-- The let-bound sibling of observeContinuousEqualsLetfree. Binding the latent
-- routes inference through the set-valued-witnesses engine instead of the InjF
-- `hasAnyExcept` combinator, and the two engines agree on the True branch (both
-- report the underlying Normal's density at the compared point) but not on its
-- complement: this program's `Left ()` is 1.0 (a single point has measure zero,
-- so its complement has measure one) where the letfree sibling's is
-- `1 - density` = 0.6479.... Pinning both makes that divergence a visible,
-- guarded fact rather than an accident -- see the task doc for why it is still
-- open.
main = observe (draw x = Normal in if x == 0.0 then 0 else 2) (\v -> v < 2)
